  "findings": [
    {
      "text": "The authors report Galactica is significantly less biased and toxic than the language models they compare.", "tone": "good",
      "source": {
        "page": "27",
        "pdfPage": 27,
        "quote": "We find Galactica is\nsignificantly less biased and toxic than existing language models."
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "[TruthfulQA](/evals/truthfulqa) accuracy stays low in absolute terms even with a curated scientific corpus.", "tone": "mixed",
      "source": {
        "page": "30",
        "pdfPage": 30,
        "quote": "However, absolute performance is still low. Given the curated nature of\nour corpus, this suggests that data alone does not cause language models to struggle at this task."
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "Paper-title citation IDs hallucinate more than alphanumeric IDs at lower model scales and low mention counts.", "tone": "mixed",
      "source": {
        "page": "8",
        "pdfPage": 8,
        "quote": "found that paper titles are more prone to hallucination error at lower scales given the text-based nature of the"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "[RealToxicityPrompts](/evals/real-toxicity-prompts) is reported only as a plot; the authors say Galactica continuations are much less toxic as prompt toxicity rises.", "tone": "good",
      "source": {
        "page": "30",
        "pdfPage": 30,
        "quote": "Galactica exhibits much lower toxicity continuation rates,\neven as we increase the original prompt toxicity."
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "The 120B model still prefers more popular papers in citation prediction, so they say it likely needs augmentation before production use.", "tone": "mixed",
      "source": {
        "page": "31",
        "pdfPage": 31,
        "quote": "some bias towards popular papers still remains with the 120B scale model, so the model likely requires"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "The authors say generations still need a verification layer to assure they are correct and factual.", "tone": "mixed",
      "source": {
        "page": "31",
        "pdfPage": 31,
        "quote": "Verification Even as language models become more accurate with scale, we need assurances that their\ngenerations are correct and factual."
      }
    }
  ],
